cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FaunaPulse in your research, please cite the software using the metadata provided below."
title: "FaunaPulse: a smartphone application for on-device detection and tracking of animals"
abstract: >-
  FaunaPulse is an offline smartphone application for monitoring animal activity
  using on-device computer vision. It detects and tracks moving organisms in real
  time using configurable object-detection models and records visits to a
  user-defined region of interest, enabling estimation of visitation frequency and
  duration. The application supports user-provided detection models,
  motion-triggered and time-lapse image capture with nocturnal monitoring. By
  performing inference directly on the smartphone, FaunaPulse enables portable and
  low-cost ecological monitoring without requiring an internet connection.
